     "explanation": "PTSD entered DSM-III in 1980. The diagnosis was driven by Vietnam veterans, antiwar psychiatrists, and feminist clinicians treating assault and incest survivors — all of whom recognized that trauma symptoms had a common pattern independent of the patient's prior personality.",
