    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Trauma Is Not the Event — It Is the Imprint",
     "content": "One of van der Kolk's most important reframes: **trauma is not the event itself. Trauma is the imprint the event leaves on body, brain, and mind.**\n\nTwo people can live through the same hurricane, the same accident, the same assault, and emerge with very different outcomes. One returns to work the next month. The other develops chronic PTSD. The difference is not how 'bad' the event was on some objective scale. It is how the nervous system processed it in the moment, and what supports were available afterward.\n\nThis insight protects survivors from the cruel question 'wasn't it really that bad?' and shifts attention to where it belongs: the lasting changes inside the person, which can be measured, treated, and changed.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Event vs. Imprint</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A small but radical reframe</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Event</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">External. Public.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Datable. Has witnesses.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Combat, accident, abuse,</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">loss, medical procedure.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">By itself, predicts</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">little about long-term harm.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"610\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Two people, same event, different outcomes.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Imprint</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Internal. Private.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Stored in body and brain.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Nervous-system tuning,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">attachment, meaning made.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">This is what therapy</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">can actually change.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"610\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Focus on the imprint, not the score.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"920\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Imprints are made — and imprints can be remade.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Healing targets the imprint, which is changeable."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "visual",
     "title": "Three Symptom Clusters",
     "content": "The PTSD diagnosis grouped trauma symptoms into three (later four) clusters. Knowing them gives you a map for everything that follows in the book.\n\n**Re-experiencing:** flashbacks, nightmares, intrusive images. The trauma keeps coming back uninvited.\n\n**Avoidance and numbing:** dodging reminders, emotional flatness, dissociation. The system tries to prevent the next intrusion by shutting down.\n\n**Hyperarousal:** insomnia, hypervigilance, irritability, exaggerated startle response. The alarm system is permanently armed.\n\nThe DSM-5 (2013) added a fourth cluster: **negative cognitions and mood** — guilt, shame, blunted joy, persistent self-blame. Together, these four clusters describe a nervous system that is both over-active and under-functioning at the same time.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The PTSD Symptom Clusters</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A map of the injury</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Re-experiencing</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Flashbacks</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Nightmares</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Intrusive sensations</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">The past invades the present.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"180\" width=\"450\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avoidance / Numbing</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Avoiding reminders</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Emotional flatness</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Dissociation</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"435\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">The system shuts down to protect itself.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"450\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hyperarousal</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"670\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Insomnia</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"705\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Hypervigilance</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Exaggerated startle</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"795\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">The alarm never gets to rest.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"540\" width=\"450\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Negative Cognition</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"670\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Guilt, shame, self-blame</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"705\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Blunted joy</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Loss of meaning</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"795\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Added in DSM-5 (2013).</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"900\" width=\"940\" height=\"150\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"975\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Over-aroused AND under-functioning at once.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Four clusters, one dysregulated system."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "What Failed: The Drug-First Era",
     "content": "The 1990s brought a wave of optimism about psychiatric drugs. Prozac arrived in 1987. The 'chemical imbalance' story dominated public conversation. Trauma survivors were prescribed SSRIs, benzodiazepines, mood stabilizers — often in heavy cocktails.\n\nVan der Kolk does not dismiss medication. SSRIs can take the edge off symptoms; sleep aids can interrupt nightmare cycles. But the drug-first model treated PTSD as a chemical problem to be corrected, and survivors as passive recipients of pills.\n\nThe results were sobering. Symptom relief was real but incomplete. Many patients felt 'flatter' rather than healed. Numbing replaced terror. And the underlying disruptions — fragmented memory, lost interoception, broken attachment — went largely untouched. The next generation of trauma research would ask a different question: not 'which drug?' but 'which experience?'",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Drug-First Era</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Useful tool, incomplete answer</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What Drugs Can Do</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">SSRIs: dampen hyperarousal</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Prazosin: cut nightmare frequency</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"385\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Benzodiazepines: short-term panic</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Symptom relief is real and not nothing.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What Drugs Don't Reach</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Fragmented traumatic memory</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Lost sense of body and self</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Broken attachment patterns</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Meaning, agency, joy</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"840\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Numbing the alarm is not healing the injury.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Pills can quiet the alarm; they don't repair the wiring."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "When van der Kolk's team scanned trauma survivors reliving their worst memories, which brain region showed reduced activity — giving rise to the phrase 'speechless terror'?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Broca's area, the brain's speech production center",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "The cerebellum, which handles balance",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "The pituitary gland, which controls hormones",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "The occipital lobe, which processes vision",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Broca's area went dark during traumatic flashbacks, while the amygdala and right hemisphere lit up. With language offline and threat circuits roaring, survivors literally could not put the experience into words — speechless terror. This finding helped justify body-based and image-based therapies that don't depend on language.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: Speechless Terror</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Which area goes dark</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"360\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Finding</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Amygdala lit up, language went out.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Survivors knew the horror;</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">they could not say it.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"460\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Broca's area produces speech.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Trauma silenced it.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"580\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"640\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Implication</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"710\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Language-only therapy is fighting</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"745\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">the injury with the missing tool.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"805\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Non-verbal routes are required.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "When words are gone, the body must lead the way."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Trace Your Own Trauma Map",
     "content": "Take twenty quiet minutes. On a sheet of paper, draw three columns: Event, Imprint, Resource. In the Event column, list one experience from your life that still has charge — small or large, recent or old. In the Imprint column, name the lasting changes you can feel: any sleep changes, body sensations, emotional patterns, beliefs about yourself or others. In the Resource column, list the people, practices, or memories that have helped quiet that imprint, even briefly. The goal is not to relive the event but to start treating yourself as a person with an imprint that can be observed, mapped, and slowly changed. This exercise becomes the personal anchor for the rest of the seminar.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Practice: Three-Column Map</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Event, Imprint, Resource</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"300\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Event</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">One experience</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">that still carries</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">charge.</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">Name it briefly,</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">don't relive it.</text><rect x=\"400\" y=\"180\" width=\"300\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Imprint</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Sleep changes</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Body sensations</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Emotional patterns</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Core beliefs</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">What lingers in</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">body and mind.</text><rect x=\"720\" y=\"180\" width=\"300\" height=\"700\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"870\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Resource</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">People</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Practices</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Places</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Memories</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">What has helped,</text><text x=\"750\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">even briefly.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"920\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Keep this map nearby across the seminar.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "A personal map you'll revisit throughout the course."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: The 5-Minute Observation Window",
     "content": "Once per day for the next week, set a five-minute timer. Sit somewhere safe. Without trying to change anything, notice: what is the rate of my breath? Where do my shoulders sit? Is my jaw tight? Where is my gaze landing? Are my hands hot, cold, neutral? Write three sentences afterward in a notebook. You are not meditating; you are gathering baseline data on your own nervous system. By the end of the week, patterns will appear: 'mornings I'm clenched,' 'after the commute my chest is tight,' 'after dinner my whole body softens.' This baseline becomes the dashboard you will use to gauge every technique you learn later in the seminar.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Practice: 5-Minute Window</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Baseline data for your own system</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Five Questions</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Rate and depth of breath</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"350\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Position of shoulders</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"390\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Tension in jaw</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Where eyes settle</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Temperature of hands</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"540\" width=\"940\" height=\"340\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Why It Matters</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">You can't regulate what you</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"695\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">cannot perceive.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"755\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Patterns appear within a week.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"815\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">This becomes your dashboard</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"850\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">for every later technique.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Five minutes a day builds the instrument you'll use for everything else."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "Which statement best captures van der Kolk's reframe of what 'trauma' actually is?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "Trauma is the imprint a stressful event leaves on body, brain, and mind — not the event itself",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "Trauma is a chemical imbalance corrected by SSRIs",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Trauma is an inherited tendency to overreact to stress",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "Trauma is any negative emotion that lasts more than a week",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Van der Kolk distinguishes the event (external, public) from the imprint (internal, lasting). Two people can live through the same event and have very different outcomes. Healing focuses on the imprint — the lasting changes in the nervous system — because that is what therapy can actually change.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quiz: What Is Trauma?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Imprint, not event</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"360\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The Reframe</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"310\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Event happened. Imprint stayed.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"355\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Therapy works on the imprint.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Same event can leave</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"450\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">very different imprints.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">No one has to justify how 'bad' it was.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"580\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"640\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clinical Implication</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"705\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Track imprints, not labels.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"745\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Imprints are made and remade</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"780\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">by lived experience.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Track imprints, change imprints."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "title": "Van der Kolk's Compass",
     "content": "Toward the end of his introduction, van der Kolk lays out the orientation that organizes the whole book:\n\n*'We have learned that trauma is not just an event that took place sometime in the past; it is also the imprint left by that experience on mind, brain, and body. This imprint has ongoing consequences for how the human organism manages to survive in the present.'*\n\nKeep this sentence in mind as we move through the next nine lessons. Every theory, every imaging study, every therapy modality you'll meet exists because the imprint is real, the imprint is measurable, and the imprint can be changed. The body keeps the score — but the score can be rewritten.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Van der Kolk's Compass</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The sentence that organizes the book</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"500\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">\"Trauma is not just an event</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">that took place sometime in the past;</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">it is also the imprint left by that</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">experience on mind, brain, and body.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">This imprint has ongoing consequences</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"530\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">for how the human organism manages</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"565\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">to survive in the present.\"</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"640\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#888\">— Bessel van der Kolk, The Body Keeps the Score</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"740\" width=\"940\" height=\"260\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Carry this forward</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"870\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Imprint is real.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"910\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Imprint is measurable.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"950\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#fff\">Imprint can be rewritten.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The compass for the next nine lessons."
     }
    }
