     "explanation": "The book's integrated thesis is that trauma is an injury to the whole organism — brain, body, nervous system, and relationships — stored largely below words. Effective treatment therefore combines bottom-up state regulation with top-down meaning-making, rests on the foundation of trauma-informed care, follows the stabilize-process-reconnect sequence, and aims ultimately at reconnection and belonging. There is no single cure and no fixed order; the clinician's art is matching, combining, and sequencing modalities to the individual.",
